1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,300
I don't need a stadium, I don't need a crowd

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,660
Just a back porch full of people who don't talk too loud

3
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,700
The kind that show up in the rain without you asking twice

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,820
With a casserole, a jumper cable, and some good advice

5
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:16,100
Like a rose bush in the springtime, you cut it back to grow

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,300
Keep the circle small, and the roots go deeper down below

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,260
Careful what you say, 'cause every word's a seed you sow

8
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:25,540
You speak it bitter, and it's bitter that's gonna grow

9
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:29,060
It only takes one match to push the dark back off the road

10
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:32,260
And one kind word can lift a stranger's heavy load

11
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:35,860
The loudest voice can grab attention it can never hold

12
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,060
But in the quiet's where the truth gets told

13
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:39,960
When pushing forward is the only road left
